      "text": "M42, a leader in artificial intelligence and digital transformation, has entered into an agreement to acquire a minority interest in @epirus  – a high-growth tech company revolutionizing national security.\n\nEpirus is on fire  right now\n\nIn June, they clinched a $43.6M contract with the U.S. Army for advanced counter-drone systems boasting longer range, greater power, and expanded capabilities.  \n\nThey've also raised $250M in Series D funding to ramp up production.  \n\nAt the core? Their Leonidas family of solid-state, software-defined high-power microwave (HPM) systems, designed to neutralize evolving electronic threats, beginning with Counter-UAS missions.\n\nThis investment spotlights @M42_AI_ 's Psychometric AI expertise and its game-changing applications in defense. \n \nBehavioral AI elevates strategic and tactical decision-making by modeling adversary behaviors and friendly responses. Revolutionizing simulations, threat detection, and mission planning.  \n\nIn training scenarios, they deliver adaptive, hyper-realistic environments based on real personnel reactions.  \n\nTargeting a $320B+ market, their approach weaves in gamification, causal inference, and complex pattern recognition for breakthroughs like:  \n\n- Advanced behavioral analytics for threat assessment  \n- Adaptive training simulations  \n- Strategic decision support systems  \n- Intelligence analysis augmentation  \n- Risk mitigation frameworks  \n\nM42 is the same company partnering with @Conste11ation and DFNN Group to launch the world's first AI, blockchain, and crypto-integrated national lottery in the Philippines – allowing users to buy regulated tickets with crypto like USDT or Bitcoin  \n\nLooking ahead, with Constellation already a leader in blockchain solutions for the Dept of War, one can't help but speculate on the potential for integrated AI-blockchain-defense ecosystems.  \n\nCould we see secure, decentralized data layers powering next-gen counter-threat systems?  \n\nThe synergies could redefine asymmetric warfare tech.",
