      "quoted_tweet": {
        "type": "tweet",
        "id": "1999887042973675725",
        "url": "https://x.com/World_At_War_6/status/1999887042973675725",
        "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/World_At_War_6/status/1999887042973675725",
        "text": "LEONIDAS: \"THE US ARMY'S NEW ANSWER TO DRONE SWARMS\"\n\nThe U.S. military has successfully tested high-power microwave weapons capable of neutralizing drone swarms in seconds.\n\nOne notable system is called Leonidas, developed by the U.S. defense firm Epirus. \n\nIn an live-fire demonstration at Camp Atterbury, Indiana, the system achieved a 100% success rate, disabling all 61 drones it engaged across five scenarios, including neutralizing a swarm of 49 drones with a single, instant pulse of electromagnetic interference.\n\nAnother system is the U.S. Air Force Research Laboratory's THOR, which also effectively counters swarms by emitting a wide beam that can take down multiple drones simultaneously.\n\nThese systems work by \"frying\" the onboard electronics of the unmanned aerial vehicles using concentrated microwave energy, a non-kinetic approach that avoids collateral damage and offers a cost-effective alternative to traditional missile defense.",
